        "motion_energy": 17.64,
        "script": "I think one of the things that we've done in the sort of more modern era is think of ourselves as separate and distinct from nature. And the more we get separated from it, the less happy we get. And the more we start acting badly. And so returning to nature, spending time in nature, is just so fundamentally important for us. In this country, 100 million people live more than a 10 minute walk from a green space. And when I say a green space, I'm not talking about this, I'm talking about just a little postage stamp of green space. And the people that live in, that can't access those areas because it's part of their natural environment, they walk to it, are generally have worse mental outcomes than people that have easy access to the outdoors. So it's critically important that we continue to push to make sure that people understand the value of nature, but even more importantly have access."
      },
